      "value": "@{67e51cce202dafbf4ae7534b|full_name}: I see these lines in your example project, i.e. RequestSerialization followed by sending a network event. Do you mean that the issue is that \"OnGameStart\" is received before the RequestSerialization arrives? If so, this was never supported. There is no timing guarantees between serialization and network events, and if you were relying on that previously, you already had a chance that this could occur due to bad network speeds of players for example.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-05-01T13:23:35.593Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "- Until now, OnDeserialization() flowed at the timing of synchronization variable changes, even in Continuous \n\n- With this append, OnDeserialization() is always running, regardless of synchronization variable changes, etc. \n\n- So even in Contiunous, explicitly Therefore, even with Contiunous, compatibility breakdown occurred in code that explicitly wrote RequestSerialization() and OnDeserialization(). \n\n・In my case, I had set Contiunous to almost Manual in terms of functionality, and it still worked fine, but with this appde It worked fine. In my case, I had it set to Contiuous, which is almost functionally Manual, and it still worked fine. I had set it to \"Contiuous\" and it still worked fine. \n\n・In my personal opinion, I think the behavior after this update is correct in terms of the name \"Contiuous\". However, I thought it would be a good idea to inform users of the compatibility breakdown that has occurred.",
